<!--
  The 10 indexable public routes. Three of the 13 built routes are deliberately
  omitted, all three noindex:

    /newsletter-thanks  reachable only from the footer newsletter form.
    /library            held back behind the coming-soon banner (31 Jul 2026).
    /wellbeing          the same.

  The two held-back pages are noindex but NOT disallowed in robots.txt, and that
  is deliberate: a page blocked from crawling cannot be read, so Google never
  sees the noindex and can keep an already-indexed URL listed indefinitely. The
  crawler has to be let in to be told to go away.

  Put /library and /wellbeing back here, and drop the `noindex` prop from both
  pages, when the app features go live.

  Keep this file in step with src/pages/ when a route is added or removed.

  Every <loc> carries a trailing slash, and that is load-bearing rather than
  cosmetic. Astro builds each route to <route>/index.html and Cloudflare Pages
  serves that at the trailing-slash URL, 308-redirecting the slash-less form to
  it. Measured on production, 31 Jul 2026:

    GET /cafe   ->  308 Permanent Redirect  ->  /cafe/
    GET /cafe/  ->  200 OK

  These entries listed the slash-less form until then, so every URL in this file
  pointed at a redirect. Keep this in step with the canonical in
  src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro — the two must agree, and both must name the URL
  that actually returns 200.
-->
